"%@ is on this iPhone, but its keys are not. That happens after restoring from a backup, because keys are locked to the phone they were made on. Enter the account's 12 or 24 words to sign in. Its history on this phone is kept." = "%@ 在这台 iPhone 上，但其密钥不在。从备份恢复后会出现这种情况，因为密钥绑定在创建它们的手机上。请输入该账户的 12 或 24 个词以登录。它在这台手机上的记录会保留。";
"Enter 12 or 24 Words" = "输入 12 或 24 个词";
"Did you create these words with a passphrase?" = "你创建这些单词时使用了密码短语吗？";
"If you are not sure, the answer is almost certainly no. A passphrase is something you would have typed in on purpose." = "如果你不确定，答案几乎肯定是没有。密码短语是你特意输入过的东西。";
"Yes" = "是";
"No" = "否";
"What is a passphrase?" = "什么是密码短语？";
"Choose your passphrase" = "设置你的密码短语";
"Write it down somewhere safe. Without it this account cannot be recovered, even with your 12 or 24 words." = "请写在安全的地方。没有它，即使有你的 12 或 24 个词，也无法恢复此账户。";
"It has to be exactly what you used before, including capital letters and spaces." = "必须与你之前用的完全一样，包括大写字母和空格。";
"Finding your address..." = "正在查找你的地址...";
"Skip the Search: Import on Address #0" = "跳过搜索：导入到地址 #0";
"Re-enter passphrase" = "再次输入密码短语";
"A passphrase is an extra word or sentence you add on top of your 12 or 24 words. It is optional, and most people do not use one." = "密码短语是在 12 或 24 个词之上额外添加的一个词或一句话。它是可选的，大多数人不会使用。";
"It does not lock your account" = "它不会锁定你的账户";
"This is the part people get wrong. A passphrase does not put a password on your account. It opens a completely different account. Your 12 or 24 words with no passphrase open one account. The same words with the word \"apple\" opens another one. With \"banana\", another one again. Every passphrase is its own separate account, with its own address and its own balance." = "这是人们最容易搞错的地方。密码短语并不是给你的账户加一个密码，而是打开一个完全不同的账户。不使用密码短语时，你的 12 或 24 个词打开一个账户；同样的单词加上 \"apple\" 会打开另一个账户，加上 \"banana\" 又是另一个。每个密码短语都是一个独立的账户，有自己的地址和余额。";
"Why anyone bothers" = "为什么有人愿意这样做";
"If someone finds your written 12 or 24 words, they get the account those words open on their own. They do not get the one behind your passphrase, because they do not know there is one, and they could not guess it anyway." = "如果有人发现了你写下的 12 或 24 个词，他们能打开仅由这些单词对应的账户，但打不开使用密码短语的那个账户，因为他们不知道它的存在，也猜不到。";
"The catch" = "需要注意";
"There is no reset and no recovery. If you forget your passphrase, the account it opened is gone for good. Your 12 or 24 words alone will not bring it back, and nobody can help you. Treat it exactly like the words themselves: written down, somewhere safe, before you rely on it." = "没有重置，也无法恢复。如果你忘记了密码短语，它所打开的账户就永远丢失了。仅凭你的 12 或 24 个词无法找回，也没有人能帮你。请像对待这些单词一样对待它：在依赖它之前，先写下来并存放在安全的地方。";
"One more thing to know" = "还有一件事需要了解";
"If you type the wrong passphrase, nothing will tell you. You will simply land in a different account, and it will look empty. That is not a bug and your money is not lost - it just means you are in the wrong account." = "如果你输入了错误的密码短语，不会有任何提示。你只会进入另一个账户，而且看起来是空的。这不是故障，你的资金也没有丢失，只是你进错了账户。";
"So do you need one?" = "那么你需要它吗？";
"If you are not sure, you do not need one: go back to the start and tap Create New Account, which makes an account without a passphrase. It is still protected by your 12 or 24 words, and you can always create another account with a passphrase later." = "如果不确定，你就不需要：返回开头并点按“创建新账户”，即可创建不带密码短语的账户。它仍受你的 12 或 24 个词保护，以后也随时可以再创建一个带密码短语的账户。";
"If you never set one up, choose No. A passphrase is something you would have typed in on purpose, so if this is the first you are hearing of it, you do not have one." = "如果你从未设置过，请选择“否”。密码短语是你有意输入的内容，如果这是你第一次听说，那就说明你没有。";
